[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Requested linear inductor model preparation

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FRONTEND-INDUCTOR-MODEL-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Resolve one constant positive flux coefficient without dropping companions
STATEMENT: >>>
Requested preparation shall resolve a scalar or L model-backed inductor into the
existing constant-inductance element. An explicit positional or named instance
inductance overrides model IND. Model L is a marker, not a multiplier. Effective
henries shall equal nominal inductance times
(1 + TC1 * deltaC + TC2 * deltaC * deltaC) times SCALE divided by M, with M and
SCALE positive and the final coefficient finite and positive. Instance TC1 and
TC2 override model coefficients. Explicit TEMP overrides DTEMP; otherwise DTEMP
is added to the circuit temperature. TNOM defaults to 27 Celsius. Temperatures
shall be physically valid. Initial current shall retain its authored amperes
without multiplicity scaling, and apply only under the existing UIC contract.
Unknown, duplicate, ambiguous or unsupported fields shall refuse atomically.
Geometry-derived, magnetic saturation and runtime-dependent inductance are not
part of this contract. Strict legacy lowering shall retain its existing profile.
<<<
